#### Shell effects on \(\beta^{-}\)-decay half-lives

Nuclear decay data provides the original and credible information of nuclear structure. It is an important topic to explore the relationship between nuclear decays and the effects of nuclear structure in nuclear physics. In this section, we focus on the shell effects on \(\beta^{-}\)-decay half-lives and discuss the relation between nuclear \(\beta^{-}\)-decay half-lives and the major shell or subshell closures.

We plot the logarithms of experimental \(\beta^{-}\)-decay half-lives along different isotopic chains near \(N=82\), \(Z=50\), \(Z=28\), and \(N=20\) closed shells in Fig. 2.20. All available

